pt input_prompt">
</div><div class=3D"inner_cell">
<div class=3D"text_cell_render border-box-sizing rendered_html">
<h3 id=3D"Importing-Matplotlib">Importing <font color=3D"#FF5733">Matplotli=
b</font><a class=3D"anchor-link" href=3D"https://htmtopdf.herokuapp.com/ipy=
nbviewer/temp/a808bfc938ddd75b0b9fd3b8dd017db2/3_plot.html?t=3D169059667732=
6#Importing-Matplotlib">=C2=B6</a></h3><p>To use matplotlib we need to impo=
rt it.We will use standard shorthand for matplotlib imports to make things =
simpler.</p>

</div>
</div>
</div>
<div class=3D"cell border-box-sizing code_cell rendered">
<div class=3D"input">
<div class=3D"prompt input_prompt">In&nbsp;[&nbsp;]:</div>
<div class=3D"inner_cell">
    <div class=3D"input_area">
<div class=3D" highlight hl-python"><pre><span></span><span class=3D"kn">im=
port</span> <span class=3D"nn">matplotlib.pyplot</span> <span class=3D"kn">=
as</span> <span class=3D"nn">plt</span>
</pre></div>

    </div>
</div>
</div>

</div>
<div class=3D"cell border-box-sizing text_cell rendered"><div class=3D"prom=
pt input_prompt">
</div><div class=3D"inner_cell">
<div class=3D"text_cell_render border-box-sizing rendered_html">
<p>Here we have imported the <strong><code>pyplot</code></strong> module fr=
om the <strong><code>matplotlib</code></strong> library as <strong><code>pl=
t</code></strong>.This is a common convention to simplify the usage of <str=
ong><code>pyplot</code></strong> functions throughout the code.</p>
<p><font color=3D"red">Basically, we'll be using **`plt`** instead of **`ma=
tplotlib.pyplot`**</font></p>

</div>
</div>
</div>
<div class=3D"cell border-box-sizing text_cell rendered"><div class=3D"prom=
pt input_prompt">
</div><div class=3D"inner_cell">
<div class=3D"text_cell_render border-box-sizing rendered_html">
<h3 id=3D"Scatterplot"><font color=3D"#FF5733">Scatterplot</font><a class=
=3D"anchor-link" href=3D"https://htmtopdf.herokuapp.com/ipynbviewer/temp/a8=
08bfc938ddd75b0b9fd3b8dd017db2/3_plot.html?t=3D1690596677326#Scatterplot">=
=C2=B6</a></h3><p><strong>Step by step guide to create a scatterplot:</stro=
ng></p>
<p><font color=3D"#FFC300 ">**Step 1:**</font></p>
<p>Firstly, we'll import the necessary packages.We'll use <code>matplotlib<=
/code> for plotting and <code>numpy</code> to produce data.</p>
<p><font color=3D"#FFC300 ">**Step 2:**</font>
Then we'll gernerate random data using numpy to plot.Here,we'll use Numpy's=
 <strong><code>random.normal()</code></strong> function to generate 100 ran=
dom numbers for two variables:<strong><code>x</code></strong> and <strong><=
code>y</code></strong></p>
<p><font color=3D"#FFC300 ">**Step 3:**</font>
 In this step we'll plot the data using matplotlib's <strong><code>scatter(=
)</code></strong> function to create a scatter plot of the <strong><code>x<=
/code></strong> and <strong><code>y</code></strong> data points.</p>
<p><strong>Syntax of scatterplot :</strong></p>

<pre><code>matplotlib.pyplot.scatter(x, y, s=3DNone, c=3DNone, marker=3DNon=
e, cmap=3DNone, norm=3DNone, vmin=3DNone, vmax=3DNone, alpha=3DNone, linewi=
dths=3DNone, *, edgecolors=3DNone, plotnonfinite=3DFalse, data=3DNone, **kw=
args)</code></pre>
<p><font color=3D"#FFC300 ">**Step 4:**</font> Finally, we use the <strong>=
<code>show()</code></strong> function to display the plot.</p>

</div>
</div>
</div>
<div class=3D"cell border-box-sizing code_cell rendered">
<div class=3D"input">
<div class=3D"prompt input_prompt">In&nbsp;[&nbsp;]:</div>
<div class=3D"inner_cell">
    <div class=3D"input_area">
<div class=3D" highlight hl-python"><pre><span></span><span class=3D"c1"># =
import packages</span>
<span class=3D"kn">import</span> <span class=3D"nn">matplotlib.pyplot</span=
> <span class=3D"kn">as</span> <span class=3D"nn">plt</span>
<span class=3D"kn">import</span> <span class=3D"nn">numpy</span> <span clas=
s=3D"kn">as</span> <span class=3D"nn">np</span>

<span class=3D"c1"># generate random data</span>
<span class=3D"n">x</span> <span class=3D"o">=3D</span> <span class=3D"n">n=
p</span><span class=3D"o">.</span><span class=3D"n">random</span><span clas=
s=3D"o">.</span><span class=3D"n">normal</span><span class=3D"p">(</span><s=
pan class=3D"n">size</span><span class=3D"o">=3D</span><span class=3D"mi">1=
00</span><span class=3D"p">)</span>
<span class=3D"n">y</span> <span class=3D"o">=3D</span> <span class=3D"n">n=
p</span><span class=3D"o">.</span><span class=3D"n">random</span><span clas=
s=3D"o">.</span><span class=3D"n">normal</span><span class=3D"p">(</span><s=
pan class=3D"n">size</span><span class=3D"o">=3D</span><span class=3D"mi">1=
00</span><span class=3D"p">)</span>

<span class=3D"c1"># plot the data</span>
<span class=3D"n">plt</span><span class=3D"o">.</span><span class=3D"n">sca=
tter</span><span class=3D"p">(</span><span class=3D"n">x</span><span class=
=3D"p">,</span> <span class=3D"n">y</span><span class=3D"p">)</span>

<span class=3D"c1"># show the plot</span>
<span class=3D"n">plt</span><span class=3D"o">.</span><span class=3D"n">sho=
w</span><span class=3D"p">()</span>
</pre></div>

    </div>
</div>
</div>

