<div class=3D"text_cell_render border-box-sizing rendered_html">
<h3 id=3D"Heatmap"><font color=3D"#FF5733">Heatmap</font><a class=3D"anchor=
-link" href=3D"https://htmtopdf.herokuapp.com/ipynbviewer/temp/a808bfc938dd=
d75b0b9fd3b8dd017db2/3_plot.html?t=3D1690596677326#Heatmap">=C2=B6</a></h3>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<div class=3D"cell border-box-sizing text_cell rendered"><div class=3D"prom=
pt input_prompt">
</div><div class=3D"inner_cell">
<div class=3D"text_cell_render border-box-sizing rendered_html">
<p>A heatmap is a graphical representation of data where values are represe=
nted as colors in a two-dimensional grid. Heatmaps are particularly useful =
for visualizing patterns, correlations, or distributions in data matrices.<=
/p>
<p>Let's see a heatmap</p>
<p><img src=3D"https://drive.google.com/uc?id=3D1jMz6IdDlDr1Ftzr_YmmXwXMa1D=
Ko3ZYQ" width=3D"600" height=3D""></p>
<p><font color=3D"#FFC300 ">**Explanation:**</font></p>
<p>Here we see a heatmap representing the harvest data of local farmers. Ea=
ch cell in the heatmap corresponds to a combination of a vegetable and a fa=
rmer, with the color intensity representing the harvest amount. The color i=
ntensity of each cell gives us the values of harvest with help of color bar=
 included.</p>

</div>
</div>
</div>
<div class=3D"cell border-box-sizing text_cell rendered"><div class=3D"prom=
pt input_prompt">
</div><div class=3D"inner_cell">
<div class=3D"text_cell_render border-box-sizing rendered_html">
<h4 id=3D"Let's-make-a-simple-Heatmap:"><strong>Let's make a simple Heatmap=
:</strong><a class=3D"anchor-link" href=3D"https://htmtopdf.herokuapp.com/i=
pynbviewer/temp/a808bfc938ddd75b0b9fd3b8dd017db2/3_plot.html?t=3D1690596677=
326#Let's-make-a-simple-Heatmap:">=C2=B6</a></h4>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<div class=3D"cell border-box-sizing text_cell rendered"><div class=3D"prom=
pt input_prompt">
</div><div class=3D"inner_cell">
<div class=3D"text_cell_render border-box-sizing rendered_html">
<p><strong>Step by step guide to create heatmap:</strong></p>
<p><font color=3D"#FFC300 ">**Step 1:**</font> Firstly, we'll import the ne=
cessary packages.We'll use <code>matplotlib</code> for plotting and <code>n=
umpy</code> to produce data.</p>
<p><font color=3D"#FFC300 ">**Step 2:**</font>Then we'll gernerate random d=
ata using numpy to plot.Here,we'll use Numpy's NumPy's <strong><code>np.ran=
dom.rand()</code></strong> function to generate  a 10x10 random matrix.</p>
<p><font color=3D"#FFC300 ">**Step 3:**</font> In this step we'll use the <=
strong><code>imshow()</code></strong> function from pyplot to create a heat=
map.The <strong><code>data</code></strong> matrix is used as the input data=
. The <strong><code>cmap</code></strong> parameter is set to <strong><code>=
autumn</code></strong> to use the autumn color map.</p>
<p><strong>Syntax of Heat map:</strong></p>

<pre><code>matplotlib.pyplot.imshow(X, cmap=3DNone, alpha=3DNone)</code></p=
re>

<pre><code>X :- this is input data matrix which is to be displayed
cmap :- Colormap we use t0 dispay the heatmap
alpha :- it specifies the opacity or transpiracy of the heatmap</code></pre=
>
<p><font color=3D"#FFC300 ">**Step 4:**</font> a color bar is then added.</=
p>
<p><font color=3D"#FFC300 ">**Step 5:**</font>we set the title and labels.<=
/p>
<p><font color=3D"#FFC300 ">**Step 6:**</font>Finally, we use the <strong><=
code>show()</code></strong> function to display the plot.</p>

</div>
</div>
</div>
<div class=3D"cell border-box-sizing code_cell rendered">
<div class=3D"input">
<div class=3D"prompt input_prompt">In&nbsp;[&nbsp;]:</div>
<div class=3D"inner_cell">
    <div class=3D"input_area">
<div class=3D" highlight hl-python"><pre><span></span><span class=3D"kn">im=
port</span> <span class=3D"nn">matplotlib.pyplot</span> <span class=3D"kn">=
as</span> <span class=3D"nn">plt</span>
<span class=3D"kn">import</span> <span class=3D"nn">numpy</span> <span clas=
s=3D"kn">as</span> <span class=3D"nn">np</span>

<span class=3D"c1"># Generate random data</span>
<span class=3D"n">data</span> <span class=3D"o">=3D</span> <span class=3D"n=
">np</span><span class=3D"o">.</span><span class=3D"n">random</span><span c=
lass=3D"o">.</span><span class=3D"n">rand</span><span class=3D"p">(</span><=
span class=3D"mi">10</span><span class=3D"p">,</span> <span class=3D"mi">10=
</span><span class=3D"p">)</span>  <span class=3D"c1"># Generate a 10x10 ra=
ndom matrix</span>

<span class=3D"c1"># Create a heatmap</span>
<span class=3D"n">plt</span><span class=3D"o">.</span><span class=3D"n">ims=
how</span><span class=3D"p">(</span><span class=3D"n">data</span><span clas=
s=3D"p">,</span> <span class=3D"n">cmap</span><span class=3D"o">=3D</span><=
span class=3D"s1">'autumn'</span><span class=3D"p">)</span>

<span class=3D"c1"># Add a color bar</span>
<span class=3D"n">plt</span><span class=3D"o">.</span><span class=3D"n">col=
orbar</span><span class=3D"p">()</span>

<span class=3D"c1"># Set title and labels</span>
<span class=3D"n">plt</span><span class=3D"o">.</span><span class=3D"n">tit=
le</span><span class=3D"p">(</span><span class=3D"s1">'Heatmap Example'</sp=
an><span class=3D"p">)</span>
<span class=3D"n">plt</span><span class=3D"o">.</span><span class=3D"n">xla=
bel</span><span class=3D"p">(</span><span class=3D"s1">'X-axis'</span><span=
 class=3D"p">)</span>
<span class=3D"n">plt</span><span class=3D"o">.</span><span class=3D"n">yla=
bel</span><span class=3D"p">(</span><span class=3D"s1">'Y-axis'</span><span=
 class=3D"p">)</span>

<span class=3D"c1"># Show the plot</span>
<span class=3D"n">plt</span><span class=3D"o">.</span><span class=3D"n">sho=
w</span><span class=3D"p">()</span>
</pre></div>

    </div>
</div>
