<div class=3D"text_cell_render border-box-sizing rendered_html">
<h3 id=3D"Boxplot"><font color=3D"#FF5733">Boxplot</font><a class=3D"anchor=
-link" href=3D"https://htmtopdf.herokuapp.com/ipynbviewer/temp/a808bfc938dd=
d75b0b9fd3b8dd017db2/3_plot.html?t=3D1690596677326#Boxplot">=C2=B6</a></h3>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<div class=3D"cell border-box-sizing text_cell rendered"><div class=3D"prom=
pt input_prompt">
</div><div class=3D"inner_cell">
<div class=3D"text_cell_render border-box-sizing rendered_html">
<p>A boxplot also known as a box and whisker plot is a graphical  represent=
ation of the distribution of a dataset.</p>
<ul>
<li>It can summarizes key statistical measures such as the median,quartiles=
, and potential outliers.
*The boxplot provides a compact way to visualize the spread and skewness of=
 the data.</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>It has the following component:</strong></p>
<p><img src=3D"https://drive.google.com/uc?id=3D19eM78CZltvykmMYu_EIhAhjV1a=
gRMybS" width=3D"400" height=3D"400"></p>
<p><font color=3D"#FFC300 ">**Box:**</font> The box represents the interqua=
rtile range (IQR), which contains the middle 50% of the data. The bottom ed=
ge of the box represents the 25th percentile (lower quartile), while the to=
p edge represents the 75th percentile (upper quartile). The line inside the=
 box represents the <strong>Median</strong>.</p>
<p><font color=3D"#FFC300 ">**Whiskers:**</font> The whiskers extend from t=
he box to the minimum and maximum non-outlier data points. They give an ide=
a of the range of the dataset, excluding any outliers.</p>
<p><font color=3D"#FFC300 ">**Outliers:**</font> Individual data points tha=
t are considered outliers are plotted as individual points outside the whis=
kers. They are typically defined as points that fall outside a certain mult=
iple of the IQR from the edges of the box.By default, the range is set to 1=
.5 times the IQR.</p>

</div>
</div>
</div>
<div class=3D"cell border-box-sizing text_cell rendered"><div class=3D"prom=
pt input_prompt">
</div><div class=3D"inner_cell">
<div class=3D"text_cell_render border-box-sizing rendered_html">
<p><strong>Step by step guide to create a boxplot:</strong></p>
<p><font color=3D"#FFC300 ">**Step 1:**</font> Firstly, we'll import the ne=
cessary packages.We'll use <code>matplotlib</code> for plotting and <code>n=
umpy</code> to produce data.</p>
<p><font color=3D"#FFC300 ">**Step 2:**</font>Then we'll gernerate random d=
ataset using numpy to plot.Here,we'll use Numpy's NumPy's <strong><code>ran=
dom.normal()</code></strong> function where the <code>loc</code> parameter =
specifies the mean of the distribution, which is set to 0 in this case. The=
 <code>scale</code> parameter specifies the standard deviation of the distr=
ibution, which is set to 1. The <code>size</code> parameter determines the =
number of data points in the dataset, which is set to 100.Then we added som=
e outliers to data and created the final data.</p>
<p><font color=3D"#FFC300 ">**Step 3:**</font> In this step we'll use the <=
strong><code>boxplot()</code></strong> function from pyplot. The <strong><c=
ode>data</code></strong> array is passed as the argument, which contains th=
e dataset to be visualized.</p>
<p><strong>Syntax of boxplot:</strong></p>

<pre><code>matplotlib.pyplot.boxplot(x, notch=3DNone, sym=3DNone, vert=3DNo=
ne, whis=3DNone, positions=3DNone, widths=3DNone, patch_artist=3DNone, boot=
strap=3DNone, usermedians=3DNone, conf_intervals=3DNone, meanline=3DNone, s=
howmeans=3DNone, showcaps=3DNone, showbox=3DNone, showfliers=3DNone, boxpro=
ps=3DNone, labels=3DNone, flierprops=3DNone, medianprops=3DNone, meanprops=
=3DNone, capprops=3DNone, whiskerprops=3DNone, manage_ticks=3DTrue, autoran=
ge=3DFalse, zorder=3DNone, capwidths=3DNone, *, data=3DNone)</code></pre>
<p><font color=3D"#FFC300 ">**Step 4:**</font>We add title and labels.</p>
<p><font color=3D"#FFC300 ">**Step 5:**</font>Finally, we use the <strong><=
code>show()</code></strong> function to display the plot.</p>

</div>
</div>
</div>
<div class=3D"cell border-box-sizing code_cell rendered">
<div class=3D"input">
<div class=3D"prompt input_prompt">In&nbsp;[&nbsp;]:</div>
<div class=3D"inner_cell">
    <div class=3D"input_area">
<div class=3D" highlight hl-python"><pre><span></span><span class=3D"kn">im=
port</span> <span class=3D"nn">matplotlib.pyplot</span> <span class=3D"kn">=
as</span> <span class=3D"nn">plt</span>
<span class=3D"kn">import</span> <span class=3D"nn">numpy</span> <span clas=
s=3D"kn">as</span> <span class=3D"nn">np</span>

<span class=3D"c1"># Generating random data</span>
<span class=3D"n">data</span> <span class=3D"o">=3D</span> <span class=3D"n=
">np</span><span class=3D"o">.</span><span class=3D"n">random</span><span c=
lass=3D"o">.</span><span class=3D"n">normal</span><span class=3D"p">(</span=
><span class=3D"n">loc</span><span class=3D"o">=3D</span><span class=3D"mi"=
>0</span><span class=3D"p">,</span> <span class=3D"n">scale</span><span cla=
ss=3D"o">=3D</span><span class=3D"mi">1</span><span class=3D"p">,</span> <s=
pan class=3D"n">size</span><span class=3D"o">=3D</span><span class=3D"mi">1=
00</span><span class=3D"p">)</span>

<span class=3D"c1"># Adding outliers</span>
<span class=3D"n">outliers</span> <span class=3D"o">=3D</span> <span class=
=3D"n">np</span><span class=3D"o">.</span><span class=3D"n">array</span><sp=
an class=3D"p">([</span><span class=3D"o">-</span><span class=3D"mi">3</spa=
n><span class=3D"p">,</span> <span class=3D"mi">3</span><span class=3D"p">]=
)</span>  <span class=3D"c1"># Example outliers</span>
<span class=3D"c1"># Final data</span>
<span class=3D"n">data_with_outliers</span> <span class=3D"o">=3D</span> <s=
pan class=3D"n">np</span><span class=3D"o">.</span><span class=3D"n">concat=
enate</span><span class=3D"p">((</span><span class=3D"n">data</span><span c=
lass=3D"p">,</span> <span class=3D"n">outliers</span><span class=3D"p">))</=
span>

<span class=3D"c1"># Create a boxplot</span>
<span class=3D"n">plt</span><span class=3D"o">.</span><span class=3D"n">box=
plot</span><span class=3D"p">(</span><span class=3D"n">data_with_outliers</=
span><span class=3D"p">)</span>

<span class=3D"c1"># Set title and labels</span>
<span class=3D"n">plt</span><span class=3D"o">.</span><span class=3D"n">tit=
le</span><span class=3D"p">(</span><span class=3D"s1">'Boxplot Example'</sp=
an><span class=3D"p">)</span>
<span class=3D"n">plt</span><span class=3D"o">.</span><span class=3D"n">xla=
bel</span><span class=3D"p">(</span><span class=3D"s1">'Data'</span><span c=
lass=3D"p">)</span>

<span class=3D"c1"># Show the plot</span>
<span class=3D"n">plt</span><span class=3D"o">.</span><span class=3D"n">sho=
w</span><span class=3D"p">()</span>
</pre></div>

    </div>
