<div class=3D"text_cell_render border-box-sizing rendered_html">
<h1 id=3D"-3.-Plotting-Contourplot-using-Precipitation-data"><font color=3D=
"blue"> 3. Plotting Contourplot using Precipitation data</font><a class=3D"=
anchor-link" href=3D"https://htmtopdf.herokuapp.com/ipynbviewer/temp/a808bf=
c938ddd75b0b9fd3b8dd017db2/3_plot.html?t=3D1690596677326#-3.-Plotting-Conto=
urplot-using-Precipitation-data">=C2=B6</a></h1>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<div class=3D"cell border-box-sizing text_cell rendered"><div class=3D"prom=
pt input_prompt">
</div><div class=3D"inner_cell">
<div class=3D"text_cell_render border-box-sizing rendered_html">
<p>Now, its time to plot a real climate data with everything you learned ea=
rlier. For this, we use <a href=3D"https://drive.google.com/file/d/1Q5mzA7a=
DhRA2baMLZ71eio-ZFHQ3mGNN/view?usp=3Dsharing">2022 Precipitation data</a> o=
ver Bangladesh and its sorrounding region.</p>

</div>
</div>
</div>
<div class=3D"cell border-box-sizing text_cell rendered"><div class=3D"prom=
pt input_prompt">
</div><div class=3D"inner_cell">
<div class=3D"text_cell_render border-box-sizing rendered_html">
<h2 id=3D"importing-libraries.">importing libraries.<a class=3D"anchor-link=
" href=3D"https://htmtopdf.herokuapp.com/ipynbviewer/temp/a808bfc938ddd75b0=
b9fd3b8dd017db2/3_plot.html?t=3D1690596677326#importing-libraries.">=C2=B6<=
/a></h2>
</div>
</div>
</div>
