<div class=3D"text_cell_render border-box-sizing rendered_html">
<h4 id=3D"Qualitative-Color-Maps:">Qualitative Color Maps:<a class=3D"ancho=
r-link" href=3D"https://htmtopdf.herokuapp.com/ipynbviewer/temp/a808bfc938d=
dd75b0b9fd3b8dd017db2/3_plot.html?t=3D1690596677326#Qualitative-Color-Maps:=
">=C2=B6</a></h4><ul>
<li>Qualitative color maps are used to represent categorical or discrete da=
ta without an inherent order or progression.</li>
<li>They are suitable for visualizing data such as different classes or cat=
egories, where the color assignment does not convey any quantitative inform=
ation.</li>
<li>Qualitative color maps have a set of distinct colors with no specific o=
rdering.
Examples of qualitative color maps include "tab10", "tab20", and "Set3".</l=
i>
<li>Qualitative color maps are often used in <strong>bar charts, pie charts=
, and scatter plots</strong> to differentiate different groups or categorie=
s.</li>
</ul>
<p><img src=3D"https://drive.google.com/uc?id=3D1XTTj6ob-iog42j3owBC_JkWSvw=
XduqkG" width=3D"" height=3D"150"></p>

</div>
</div>
</div>
<div class=3D"cell border-box-sizing text_cell rendered"><div class=3D"prom=
pt input_prompt">
</div><div class=3D"inner_cell">
<div class=3D"text_cell_render border-box-sizing rendered_html">
<h5 id=3D"Example">Example<a class=3D"anchor-link" href=3D"https://htmtopdf=
.herokuapp.com/ipynbviewer/temp/a808bfc938ddd75b0b9fd3b8dd017db2/3_plot.htm=
l?t=3D1690596677326#Example">=C2=B6</a></h5>
</div>
</div>
</div>
<div class=3D"cell border-box-sizing code_cell rendered">
<div class=3D"input">
<div class=3D"prompt input_prompt">In&nbsp;[&nbsp;]:</div>
<div class=3D"inner_cell">
    <div class=3D"input_area">
<div class=3D" highlight hl-python"><pre><span></span><span class=3D"kn">im=
port</span> <span class=3D"nn">matplotlib.pyplot</span> <span class=3D"kn">=
as</span> <span class=3D"nn">plt</span>
<span class=3D"kn">import</span> <span class=3D"nn">numpy</span> <span clas=
s=3D"kn">as</span> <span class=3D"nn">np</span>

<span class=3D"c1"># Generate random data</span>
<span class=3D"n">x</span> <span class=3D"o">=3D</span> <span class=3D"n">n=
p</span><span class=3D"o">.</span><span class=3D"n">linspace</span><span cl=
ass=3D"p">(</span><span class=3D"mi">0</span><span class=3D"p">,</span> <sp=
an class=3D"mi">10</span><span class=3D"p">,</span> <span class=3D"mi">100<=
/span><span class=3D"p">)</span>
<span class=3D"n">y</span> <span class=3D"o">=3D</span> <span class=3D"n">n=
p</span><span class=3D"o">.</span><span class=3D"n">sin</span><span class=
=3D"p">(</span><span class=3D"n">x</span><span class=3D"p">)</span>

<span class=3D"c1"># Create a qualitative color map</span>
<span class=3D"n">cmap</span> <span class=3D"o">=3D</span> <span class=3D"s=
1">'Set3'</span>

<span class=3D"c1"># Plot the data using the color map</span>
<span class=3D"n">plt</span><span class=3D"o">.</span><span class=3D"n">sca=
tter</span><span class=3D"p">(</span><span class=3D"n">x</span><span class=
=3D"p">,</span> <span class=3D"n">y</span><span class=3D"p">,</span> <span =
class=3D"n">c</span><span class=3D"o">=3D</span><span class=3D"n">y</span><=
span class=3D"p">,</span> <span class=3D"n">cmap</span><span class=3D"o">=
=3D</span><span class=3D"n">cmap</span><span class=3D"p">)</span>

<span class=3D"c1"># Add a color bar</span>
<span class=3D"n">plt</span><span class=3D"o">.</span><span class=3D"n">col=
orbar</span><span class=3D"p">()</span>

<span class=3D"c1"># Set title and labels</span>
<span class=3D"n">plt</span><span class=3D"o">.</span><span class=3D"n">tit=
le</span><span class=3D"p">(</span><span class=3D"s1">'Qualitative Color Ma=
p Example'</span><span class=3D"p">)</span>
<span class=3D"n">plt</span><span class=3D"o">.</span><span class=3D"n">xla=
bel</span><span class=3D"p">(</span><span class=3D"s1">'X-axis'</span><span=
 class=3D"p">)</span>
<span class=3D"n">plt</span><span class=3D"o">.</span><span class=3D"n">yla=
bel</span><span class=3D"p">(</span><span class=3D"s1">'Y-axis'</span><span=
 class=3D"p">)</span>

<span class=3D"c1"># Show the plot</span>
<span class=3D"n">plt</span><span class=3D"o">.</span><span class=3D"n">sho=
w</span><span class=3D"p">()</span>
</pre></div>

